{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And its livestock by the sword.</b> To blot out their memory, as an act of vengeance on behalf of the blessed El — as in the case of Amalek, as it says: תִּמְחֶה אֶת זֵכֶר עֲמָלֵק (Deuteronomy 25:19). So too the prophet explained, in saying: וְהֵמַתָּה מֵאִישׁ עַד אִשָּׁה מֵעוֹלֵל וְעַד יוֹנֵק מִשּׁוֹר וְעַד שֶׂה מִגָּמָל וְעַד חֲמוֹר (1 Samuel 15:3)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:24.222474216Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}